    <section class="documentation-section" id="Implementation">
        <h2 class="documentation-header">3. Implementation</h2>

        <h3 class="documentation-subheader">3.1 Application Structure Overview</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><b>Entry Point & Configuration (<code>Program.cs</code>):</b> Configures the web server, MVC, session
                state, static file serving, and registers services such as the Cart and database context. Sets up the
                HTTP request pipeline, routing, and middleware order.</li>
            <li><b>Controllers (<code>Controllers/</code>):</b> Handle incoming web requests, interact with models and
                services, and select views to render. Includes controllers for computers, components, cart, customer
                management (registration, login, password recovery), and order management (view, edit, delete orders).
            </li>
            <li><b>Models (<code>Models/</code>):</b> Represent the application's data entities, such as
                <code>Computer</code>, <code>Component</code>, <code>Customer</code>, <code>Order</code>, and
                <code>OrderItem</code>. Models encapsulate business logic and structure for all store data.
            </li>
            <li><b>ViewModels (<code>ViewModels/</code>):</b> Shape and combine data for specific views, often
                aggregating multiple models (e.g., <code>CustomizeComputerViewModel</code>,
                <code>OrderDetailsViewModel</code>).
            </li>
            <li><b>Views (<code>Views/</code>):</b> Razor <code>.cshtml</code> files define the HTML structure and
                presentation. Organized by controller and action. Shared layout and error pages are in
                <code>Views/Shared/</code>.
            </li>
            <li><b>Areas (<code>Areas/</code>):</b> Used to organize related functionality into separate sections of the
                application, such as Identity for authentication and user management. Areas help keep large projects
                organized by grouping controllers, views, and models for specific modules (like account management) into
                their own folders. This makes it easier to maintain and extend features like login, registration, and
                password recovery, and is required for ASP.NET Core Identity scaffolding.</li>
            <li><b>Data Access (<code>Data/</code>):</b> Contains the Entity Framework Core <code>DbContext</code>
                class, which manages all database access for products, components, customers, and orders. Database
                migrations and seeding are handled here.</li>
            <li><b>Static Assets (<code>wwwroot/</code>):</b> Contains CSS, JavaScript, images, and client-side
                libraries for styling and interactivity.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="documentation-subheader">3.2 Key Features Implementation</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><b>Database Integration:</b> All product, component, customer, and order data is stored and managed in a
                SQL database using Entity Framework Core. The <code>DbContext</code> is configured in
                <code>Program.cs</code> and injected into controllers.
            </li>
            <li><b>Customer Management:</b> Registration, authentication, and password recovery are implemented using
                secure, database-backed modules. Passwords are hashed and stored securely. Customers can register, log
                in, and reset forgotten passwords via email verification.</li>
            <li><b>Order Management:</b> Registered customers can view, edit, and delete their orders. When an order is
                submitted, all details (including selected components and pricing) are saved in the database and
                displayed in a confirmation view. Customers can manage their order history through a dedicated
                interface.</li>
            <li><b>Product Catalog & Customization:</b> Catalog data is loaded from the database. Users can browse
                computers, view details, and customize builds by selecting compatible components. The total price
                updates dynamically as selections change.</li>
            <li><b>Cart & Session State:</b> For anonymous users, cart contents are tracked using cookies or session.
                For registered users, cart and order data are persisted in the database. Cart management logic ensures a
                seamless experience across sessions and logins.</li>
            <li><b>Navigation & Pages:</b> The site includes all required pages: splash/home, component list, component
                details, cart, checkout, order confirmation, contact, feedback, and customer/order management. All
                navigation links and buttons are active and functional.</li>
            <li><b>Dynamic Updates:</b> JavaScript is used for real-time price calculation and UI updates during
                customization and checkout.</li>
            <li><b>Security:</b> User authentication, authorization, and input validation are enforced throughout the
                application. Sensitive operations (like order management) require the user to be logged in.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="documentation-subheader">3.3 Notable Implementation Details</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><b>Entity Framework Core:</b> Used for all data access, migrations, and database schema management.
                Models are mapped to database tables, and relationships (such as orders and order items) are defined
                using navigation properties.</li>
            <li><b>Separation of Concerns:</b> The MVC pattern is strictly followed, with controllers handling logic,
                models representing data, and views managing presentation.</li>
            <li><b>Extensibility:</b> The codebase is organized to allow easy addition of new features, such as more
                component types, advanced customer features, or additional payment and shipping modules.</li>
            <li><b>Validation:</b> Both client-side and server-side validation are implemented for forms (registration,
                login, feedback, etc.) to ensure data integrity and security.</li>
            <li><b>Responsive Design:</b> CSS and layout techniques ensure usability on both desktop and mobile devices.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="documentation-section" id="UserGuide">
        <h2 class="documentation-header">4. User Guide</h2>

        <h3 class="documentation-subheader">4.1 Getting Started</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Open the Computer Builder web application in your browser (locally or on the server where it is
                deployed).</li>
            <li>Navigate to the homepage to view the store branding, welcome message, and navigation menu.</li>
            <li>Use the navigation menu to browse the catalog of available computers and components.</li>
            <li>Select a computer to view its details and begin customization.</li>
            <li>Choose your preferred components (RAM, hard drive, CPU, etc.) from the dropdown lists. The total price
                will update automatically as you make changes.</li>
            <li>Once satisfied, click the "Add to Cart" button to save your customized build.</li>
            <li>Go to the Cart page to review your selections and see a summary of your configuration and pricing.</li>
            <li>If you are a new user, register for an account to enable order management and persistent cart storage.
            </li>
            <li>Log in to your account to access order history, manage your orders, and use password recovery if needed.
            </li>
            <li>Proceed to checkout to finalize your order. Registered users will have their order details saved in the
                database and can view, edit, or delete orders later.</li>
            <li>Use the Contact or Feedback pages to reach out or provide comments if needed.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3 class="documentation-subheader">4.2 Features Overview</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><b>Storefront Navigation:</b> Access all main pages (Home, Catalog, Cart, Contact, Feedback,
                Documentation, Account, Orders) from the top/bottom navigation menu.</li>
            <li><b>Product Catalog:</b> Browse a list of computers and components, each with detailed information and
                pricing, all loaded from the database.</li>
            <li><b>Customization:</b> Select and swap compatible components for each computer, with real-time price
                updates.</li>
            <li><b>Cart Summary:</b> View a detailed summary of your customized build and total price before checkout.
            </li>
            <li><b>Session Tracking:</b> For anonymous users, selections and cart are saved using cookies or session.
                For registered users, cart and order data are persisted in the database.</li>
            <li><b>Customer Management:</b> Register, log in, and recover your password securely. All customer data is
                managed in the database.</li>
            <li><b>Order Management:</b> Registered users can view, edit, and delete their orders. Order details,
                including selected components and pricing, are saved and managed in the database.</li>
            <li><b>Contact & Feedback:</b> Submit questions or feedback through dedicated forms, with validation for
                required fields.</li>
            <li><b>Responsive Design:</b> The site is usable on both desktop and mobile devices.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="documentation-subheader">4.3 Notes for Users</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>If you clear your browser cookies, your cart and selections will be reset (for anonymous users).</li>
            <li>Registered users benefit from persistent cart and order management, even across devices.</li>
            <li>All navigation links and buttons are active and functional.</li>
            <li>For best experience, use a modern browser (Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Safari).</li>
            <li>Contact and feedback forms require all fields to be filled out before submission.</li>
            <li>For password recovery, follow the instructions sent to your registered email address.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

